#: ../../../cute/build-with-cutlass.md:1
msgid "Build with the CUTLASS Compiler"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../cute/build-with-cutlass.md:3
msgid ""
"CuTe kernels compile through NVIDIA's CUTLASS 4.8.1 compiler library rather "
"than the native LLVM path. `cargo oxide` installs the pinned release once, "
"verifies its SHA-256 digest on every load, and embeds the resulting cubin "
"straight into your Rust binary."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../cute/build-with-cutlass.md:7
msgid ""
"Rust kernel (`cute-rs`)\n"
"  ──►  one Pliron module: dialect-cute, dialect-mir, dialect-nvvm\n"
"  ──►  whole-module verification and the target gate\n"
"  ──►  exporter profile (`cuda-oxide-mlir-export`)\n"
"  ──►  libCutlassCompiler 4.8.1 (`x86_64-cu13` or `aarch64-cu13`)\n"
"  ──►  cubin embedded in the host binary\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../cute/build-with-cutlass.md:16
msgid "Install once"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../cute/build-with-cutlass.md:18
msgid "cargo oxide toolchain install cutlass\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../cute/build-with-cutlass.md:22
msgid ""
"Downloads the official CUTLASS 4.8.1 release archive from GitHub and "
"verifies both the archive and `libCutlassCompiler.so` SHA-256 digests. The "
"bundle is covered by the NVIDIA EULA, which the installer prints before "
"downloading."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../cute/build-with-cutlass.md:25
msgid ""
"Supports both **Linux `x86_64`** and **Linux `aarch64`** (including Grace-"
"Blackwell and Vera-Rubin ARM nodes) with CUDA 13. The library lands in "
"Cargo's data directory under `cuda-oxide/toolchains/cutlass/4.8.1/{x86_64-"
"cu13,aarch64-cu13}`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../cute/build-with-cutlass.md:28
msgid ""
"`CUDA_OXIDE_CUTLASS_COMPILER=/abs/path/libCutlassCompiler.so` overrides "
"discovery. The digest check still runs, so only the byte-identical 4.8.1 "
"library loads."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../cute/build-with-cutlass.md:31
msgid "How CUTLASS upgrades stay compatible"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../cute/build-with-cutlass.md:33
msgid ""
"CUTLASS's internal MLIR ops are not a stable public IR: minor CUTLASS "
"releases routinely rename op properties (such as `mmaKind` to `kind` or "
"`scaleVecSize` to `blockScale`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../cute/build-with-cutlass.md:36
msgid ""
"That is why `cargo oxide` pairs the SHA-pinned compiler with an **exporter "
"profile** in `cuda-oxide-mlir-export`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../cute/build-with-cutlass.md:38
msgid ""
"Your Rust kernel compiles into `dialect-cute` and `dialect-nvvm`, which are "
"owned by `cuda-oxide` and stay stable across CUTLASS bumps."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../cute/build-with-cutlass.md:40
msgid ""
"All CUTLASS-version-specific MLIR spelling lives inside the exporter "
"profile, so moving from CUTLASS 4.7 to 4.8.1 requires **zero edits** to "
"existing Rust kernels."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../cute/build-with-cutlass.md:42
msgid ""
"Host crates (`cuda-core`, `cuda-bindings`, `cuda-async`) have zero "
"dependency on `cute-rs` or the CUTLASS compiler and are versioned "
"independently."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../cute/build-with-cutlass.md:45
msgid "Build and run"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../cute/build-with-cutlass.md:47
msgid ""
"CUDA_OXIDE_DEVICE_BACKEND=cutlass-mlir cargo oxide run elementwise_cute --"
"arch sm_120a\n"
"CUDA_OXIDE_DEVICE_BACKEND=cutlass-mlir cargo oxide build "
"fp16_gemm_256x352_cute --arch sm_100a\n"
"CUDA_OXIDE_DEVICE_BACKEND=cutlass-mlir cargo oxide run sm107_mxfp8_gemm_cute "
"--arch sm_107a\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../cute/build-with-cutlass.md:53
msgid ""
"Every CuTe kernel needs `CUDA_OXIDE_DEVICE_BACKEND=cutlass-mlir`. The native "
"backend has no CuTe lowering and stops with a verification error."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../cute/build-with-cutlass.md:55
msgid ""
"Four validated targets: `sm_100a` (Blackwell B200), `sm_103a` (Blackwell "
"Ultra B300), `sm_107a` (Vera Rubin), and `sm_120a` (RTX 50 series). Anything "
"else is rejected before compilation with an error naming the target. Within "
"that set, `tcgen05` operations need `sm_100a`, `sm_103a`, or `sm_107a`; "
"SM107 `MXF8F6F4` block-scaled MMA needs `sm_107a`; and MXF4 register MMA "
"needs `sm_120a`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../cute/build-with-cutlass.md:60
msgid ""
"`cargo oxide run` without `--arch` uses the detected GPU, so an RTX 5090 "
"selects `sm_120a` and a Vera Rubin GPU selects `sm_107a`. `cargo oxide "
"build` needs `--arch`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../cute/build-with-cutlass.md:62
msgid ""
"Each example README states its device and shape requirements. The [support "
"matrix](support-matrix.md) lists what each target covers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../cute/build-with-cutlass.md:65
msgid "Options"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../cute/build-with-cutlass.md:67
msgid "Variable"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../cute/build-with-cutlass.md:67
msgid "Purpose"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../cute/build-with-cutlass.md:67
msgid "`CUDA_OXIDE_DEVICE_BACKEND`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../cute/build-with-cutlass.md:69
msgid "`native` (default) or `cutlass-mlir`; other values fail"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../cute/build-with-cutlass.md:69
msgid "`CUDA_OXIDE_MLIR_PROFILE`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../cute/build-with-cutlass.md:70
msgid ""
"`cutlass-full-cute-mlir22` (default) or `cutlass-primitives-mlir22` (`*_ctm`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../cute/build-with-cutlass.md:70
msgid "`CUDA_OXIDE_CUTLASS_OPT_LEVEL`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../cute/build-with-cutlass.md:71
msgid "`2` or `3` (default); included in the build fingerprint"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../cute/build-with-cutlass.md:71
msgid "`CUDA_OXIDE_MLIR_OUTPUT`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../cute/build-with-cutlass.md:72
msgid "Path for the prepared MLIR text, for example `$PWD/module.mlir`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../cute/build-with-cutlass.md:72
msgid "`CUDA_OXIDE_CUTLASS_COMPILER`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../cute/build-with-cutlass.md:73
msgid ""
"Absolute path to a `libCutlassCompiler.so` matching the pinned 4.8.1 digest"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../cute/build-with-cutlass.md:75
msgid ""
"`CUDA_OXIDE_BACKEND` selects the rustc backend library, not the device path. "
"Keep MLIR dumps and cubins out of version control."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../cute/build-with-cutlass.md:78
msgid "Failures"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../cute/build-with-cutlass.md:80
msgid ""
"Unsupported operations, rejected targets, verification errors, and compiler "
"errors stop the build. There is no fallback to another backend."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../cute/build-with-cutlass.md:82
msgid ""
"The compiler checks layouts, operand roles, pipeline state, and the launch "
"ABI. It does not prove thread convergence, barrier phases, asynchronous "
"completion, or pointer lifetimes; see [Checks and Obligations](contracts.md)."
msgstr ""
